[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Read report by report, it
is not one issue. The fix queued for the parser will not fix the booking-v3 form, and neither
fix touches the reports where a date moved by one day.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is more than one bug. Each problem below has its own ticket. Closing #4471 when the parser
fix ships leaves the others open.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  issues={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/kevinw9092/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/kevinw9092/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2',
    shift: 'https://github.com/kevinw9092/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3',
  }}
/>

## How to tell them apart

- **`parser`**: the tenant writes dates day first (every tenant on file does, `en-GB` and
  `en-IE` included) and the report came in by app, by email, or through a booking-v2 form. The
  shared parser reads the date month first, so day and month swap: 4 July becomes 7 April.
- **`hint`**: the report came through the booking form on a **booking-v3** tenant. That form
  prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what it shows, month first; the form
  reads the date the tenant's way, day first. The result looks like the parser bug, so it got
  merged with it, but the fix is in the form, not the parser.
- **`shift`**: the date is one day off, not swapped. An invite one day early, every June booking
  a day off, an invite that arrived before the booking was made, a guest in Lisbon and a guest
  in Toronto shown different days for one meeting. Day/month order cannot do that; a time zone
  or offset can. The desk already noted these reports as a one-day move, then filed them under
  the tenant's cause.

Ignore the intake tag when you sort these. It is guessed from the reporter's browser locale, not
from the tenant, and it disagrees with the tenant on many reports in this ticket.

## Why one ticket

Reports were merged on matching subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
Subjects like "Date is wrong" fit all three bugs, so all three ended up here. The table the
incident page shows already splits out `hint`, but labels it "no ticket of its own":

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What to do

1. Keep #4471 for `parser` only. Track `hint` and `shift` in their own tickets (linked above).
2. Ship the booking-v3 fix with the parser fix: the hint has to match how the form reads the
   date, or `hint` reports keep coming after the parser is fixed.
3. Treat `shift` as its own investigation (time zones, offsets, the June-only pattern).
4. Replace decision 0001 with a new record: match on cause (tenant, channel, form), not subject.

